{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"polynomial factorization polynomial factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md","fileName":"Polynomial Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Polynomial Factorization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Factoring and Algebraic Identities]] · [[Polynomial Rings and Factorization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Polynomial Rings and Factorization","Factor","Polynomial Expansion","algebraessentials.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"polynomial factorization polynomial factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md","fileName":"Polynomial Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Polynomial Factorization","heading":"Polynomial Factorization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Polynomial factorization rewrites a polynomial as a product of simpler [[Factor]]s. It is the reverse of [[Polynomial Expansion]]:\n\n$$ab+ac=a(b+c).$$\n\nMethods include removing a common factor, grouping terms to expose a repeated factor, recognizing a special identity, and factoring a quadratic trinomial. A complete factorization applies methods repeatedly until the remaining factors cannot be decomposed further over the chosen number system. Multiplying the factors verifies that the original polynomial is recovered.\n\nThe modern-algebra treatment makes the coefficient field explicit because a polynomial may be reducible over one field and irreducible over another. Complete factorization is therefore always relative to the selected ring or field.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Polynomial Rings and Factorization","Factor","Polynomial Expansion","algebraessentials.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"polynomial factorization polynomial factorization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Factorization.md","fileName":"Polynomial Factorization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Polynomial Factorization","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Factoring and Algebraic Identities","Polynomial Rings and Factorization","Factor","Polynomial Expansion","algebraessentials.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}